# Project Description and Basics

## Description

This is a WordPress website for the ART/New York organization. The site customizations currently consist of a custom theme, `rhd-art-new-york`.

## Perfectmind integration
API Documentation for the Perfectmind integration is here: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1X8HgElUwBL-KHQG1eClP919hsWjlWrXx/view

## Xplor/PerfectMind API access
PERFECTMIND_BASE_URL, PERFECTMIND_API_KEY, PERFECTMIND_CLIENT_NUMBER are all defined constants.

- PERFECTMIN_BASE_URL is the remote Xplor/PerfectMind server to query.
- PERFECTMIND_REST_BASE is the REST endpoint base to query.
- PERFECTMIND_API_KEY is sent in each REST operation as the X-Access-Key header.
- PERFECTMIND_CLIENT_NUMBER is sent in each REST operation as the X-Client-Number header.

## RHD block plugins (e.g. `rhd-artny-directory`)

- Follow the pattern in `wp-content/plugins/rhd-cover-parallax-block` and `wp-content/plugins/rhd-artny-directory`: `block.json` + `render.php`, Roundhouse naming (`rhd-*`), theme-aligned markup using `wp-block-*` classes and `theme.json` CSS variables.
- **Dynamic blocks must register in the editor client-side (WP 7+).** Server-only `register_block_type()` is not enough — the editor will show “Your site doesn't include support for the block.” Register `assets/editor.js` explicitly in PHP with dependencies: `wp-blocks`, `wp-element`, `wp-block-editor`, `wp-server-side-render`, `wp-components`. Do not rely on `block.json` `"editorScript": "file:./…"` alone; auto-registered editor scripts may load with **empty deps** and fail silently.
- Use `ServerSideRender` in `edit` for editor preview of dynamic blocks. Guard `registerBlockType` with `getBlockType()` to avoid double registration.
- **Render core block output via `do_blocks()` or `render_block()`** — do not hand-roll markup for blocks that ship icons/assets (e.g. `core/social-links` needs SVG icons from core). Match demo page block attributes (icon colors, layout) when mirroring existing designs.
- When renaming a plugin: rename folder + main file, update all slugs/classes/text domains/block names, swap `active_plugins` entry, and update `<!-- wp:namespace/block -->` comments in post content. Register a legacy block name if content may still reference the old name.
- Verify on dev: plugin active, block registered after `init`, page renders expected markup (`docker exec … php -r "require wp-load.php; …"`).

## UI details in directory cards

- `<details><summary>` defaults to bold in browsers — set `font-weight: 400` (or `normal`) explicitly when summary should match body text.
- Scope card typography overrides under plugin classes (e.g. `.rhd-artny-directory__card .wp-block-details`) using theme font-size presets (`--wp--preset--font-size--small`).

## Accessible multi-select filter dropdowns

When replacing checkbox groups with compact multi-select filters (directory block and similar RHD UI):

- **Pattern:** disclosure button + panel of checkboxes — not `<select multiple>` (modifier keys) and not listbox without full ARIA support.
- **Markup:** visible group label (`id` on label span) → `.filter-dropdown-control` wrapper (positioned) → `type="button"` trigger + `hidden` panel with checkboxes. Keep existing `data-*-filter` attributes on inputs so client-side `readFilters()` stays unchanged.
- **Trigger ARIA:** `aria-labelledby="{label-id} {summary-id}"` so the accessible name includes **both** the group name and current selection. Give the summary span its own `id`; update its `textContent` in JS. Add `aria-haspopup="true"`, `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`. Do **not** put `aria-live` inside the button — it fights `aria-labelledby` and causes duplicate announcements.
- **Panel ARIA:** `role="group"` + `aria-labelledby` on the group label only. Avoid redundant `<fieldset>`/`<legend>` inside the panel when the group is already labeled.
- **Keyboard / behavior:** Enter/Space opens; Escape closes and returns focus to trigger; click outside closes; only one panel open at a time. Checkboxes must not be in tab order when panel is `hidden`.
- **Status / empty states:** Result counts and **zero-result messages** must go through an existing `role="status" aria-live="polite"` region. Do not clear the live region and rely on a separate static empty element alone. If a visible empty message remains for sighted users, mark it `aria-hidden="true"` when the live region carries the announcement.
- **Helper copy:** Associate instructional text with the form via `aria-describedby`.
- **Verification:** Do not treat accessible UI as complete from markup/implementation alone. Run structured verification (live page DOM, keyboard paths, accessible names) before sign-off; fix Major WCAG gaps (4.1.2 Name/Role/Value, 4.1.3 Status Messages) before claiming AA-ready.
